    "q-175353": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175353",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is divisible by $3,$\n\nwhere the universal set is the set of integers from $5$ to $20$ inclusive.",
      "worked_solution": "The *truth set* $T$ of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is\n\n$$\nU=\\{5,6,…,20\\}.\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nThe following numbers give the elements of our truth set:\n\n- $x=6$ since $6$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=9$ since $9$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=12$ since $12$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=15$ since $15$ is divisible by $3,$\n\n- $x=18$ since $18$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=\\{6,9,12,15,18\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
