    "q-175358": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175358",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $4x-3\\ge 9,$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$",
      "worked_solution": "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $4x-3\\ge 9$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nNow, we need to solve the above inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3\\ge 9 \\\\ 4x\\ge 12 \\\\ x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=[3,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-175358-a",
